WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:07.359
We’re following a member of a private and
controversial border watch organization “Minute

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:08.359
Men”.

00:00:08.359 --> 00:00:13.800
Robert Crooks, a 67-year old retiree from
Las Vegas patrols the US-Mexican border in

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.450
the Campo area,north of San Diego.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.750
Crooks has been doing this for about a month
now…

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.900
every day.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.810
He lives and sleeps in his pick-up truck – AND
he patrols, watches, and tracks, what he calls

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.289
invaders and enemies of the United States
of America.

00:00:30.289 --> 00:00:32.300
“They are not coming this way.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.359
And if the do I'll be waiting for them watching.

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:38.719
They’re not sneaking in.”

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:43.379
Roberts joined the “Minute Men Project”
- a group that many describe as a dangerous

00:00:43.379 --> 00:00:45.219
militia - in 2005.

00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:49.670
He says, even back then he felt he needed
to help secure the border and fight off what

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.590
he calls an invasion of illegal immigrants.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.789
“It’s my country, it’s your country,
it’s our country.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.710
You know, if nobody makes a stand, we wouldn’t
have a country.”

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.329
He sees himself as a patriot.

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:06.850
He claimed this hilltop overseeing the border
for himself by installing a flag pole.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:07.890
This is his base.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.310
He named it “Point Patriot”.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:14.890
It is here where - in his view - he serves
his country at a critical time.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:19.010
Where he makes a stand in what he calls the
epic battle against illegal immigrants.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:22.010
“This is a defining moment in history right
now.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:27.360
If we don't do something here today, this,
you know right now, this could be, it's got

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.040
the ramifications of turning into something
very dangerous to our nation.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.720
If we start allowing hoards of thousands and
thousands just to cross the border, crush

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.760
our cities you know, that's a recipe for disaster
you know.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.100
It has to stop here.”

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.740
For all of the “criminals in Tijuana”,
as he calls the Caravan migrants from Central

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:57.650
America sheltered on the other side of the
border, Robert has this message:

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:07.300
“They have to go back home.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.200
…America is full.”

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.790
The Federal Agents of the US Border Patrol
do NOT necessarily agree with any of Crook’s

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.790
sentiments.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.379
However, out here in the field they do appreciate
him patrolling the area, watching and alerting

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:24.870
them to suspicious movements from the other
side.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.599
That’s enough of a reward for this Minute
man.

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:31.370
“As long as this is going on, I will be
involved.”

